      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A four-hour telemetry lag will introduce a significant delay in the adaptive response to sudden, regionally isolated crises or opportunities. For critical redistribution of life-saving meds, this delay means the system will be operating on outdated constraint data, potentially leading to localized stockouts or massive overstocking before any corrective action is initiated. Essentially, the increased resilience at the local level is offset by a major reduction in proactive, global optimization capability during those four-hour windows.",
      "source": "target",
